Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:19:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Decrypt /data: a VINTF manifest TWRP can read; TrustZone
 apps from apnhlos

Found by running the services by hand in the second decryption build:

- The tablet's vendor manifest is manifest.version 8.0 with sepolicy
  202404; TWRP 12.1's libvintf (4.0) rejects the whole file, so neither
  KeyMint nor gatekeeper may register ('Could not find ...
  IKeyMintDevice/default in the VINTF manifest', KeyMint aborts). Use a
  small manifest with only the entries decryption needs (gatekeeper,
  strongbox keymaster, Samsung KeyMint extension/factory; KeyMint itself
  in manifest/), copied from the tablet's.
- KeyMint then failed 'QSEECom_start_app failed': its TrustZone app
  (skeymast.mdt/.bNN) is on the apnhlos partition, which Android mounts
  at /vendor/firmware_mnt. That directory holds the ramdisk's touchscreen
  firmware here, so gts9wifi-ta-links.sh mounts apnhlos read-only at
  /mnt/apnhlos and links its images in (on post-fs).

With both, by hand: qseecomd, KeyMint ('successfully load skeymint',
SKeyMint 200.0.72), gatekeeper and keystore2 all run.
---
 recovery/root/init.recovery.keymint.rc        |   3 +
 recovery/root/system/bin/gts9wifi-ta-links.sh |  11 +
 recovery/root/vendor/etc/vintf/manifest.xml   | 240 +-----------------
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 233 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 recovery/root/system/bin/gts9wifi-ta-links.sh

diff --git a/recovery/root/init.recovery.keymint.rc b/recovery/root/init.recovery.keymint.rc
index 24c0e48..d38f7c0 100644
--- a/recovery/root/init.recovery.keymint.rc
+++ b/recovery/root/init.recovery.keymint.rc
@@ -4,6 +4,9 @@
 # service (with Samsung's libskeymint10device), started the same way:
 # once qseecomd has registered its listeners, stopped after decryption.
 
+on post-fs
+    exec u:r:recovery:s0 root root -- /system/bin/sh /system/bin/gts9wifi-ta-links.sh
+
 service keymint-qti /system/bin/android.hardware.security.keymint-service-qti
     user root
     group root drmrpc
diff --git a/recovery/root/system/bin/gts9wifi-ta-links.sh b/recovery/root/system/bin/gts9wifi-ta-links.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..bee78c1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/recovery/root/system/bin/gts9wifi-ta-links.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+#!/system/bin/sh
+# The TrustZone apps (KeyMint's "skeymast", gatekeeper, ...) live on the
+# apnhlos partition, which Android mounts at /vendor/firmware_mnt.  Here
+# that directory already holds the touchscreen/keyboard firmware of the
+# ramdisk, so mount apnhlos read-only elsewhere and link its images in.
+mkdir -p /mnt/apnhlos
+mount -t vfat -o ro /dev/block/bootdevice/by-name/apnhlos /mnt/apnhlos || exit 1
+for f in /mnt/apnhlos/image/*; do
+	n=/vendor/firmware_mnt/image/${f##*/}
+	[ -e "$n" ] || ln -s "$f" "$n"
+done
